# HomeOps mobile env — copy to .env.local for a physical device, or let
# `npm run dev-client` set it for you (it writes your PC's current LAN IP).
#
# The mobile app reads exactly one variable:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL — the HomeOps backend base URL the phone should call.
#     • Deployed backend (the default below): https://homeops-ai.onrender.com/
#     • Simulator / web against a LOCAL server: http://localhost:8787
#     • Physical iPhone on the same Wi-Fi:      http://<YOUR-PC-LAN-IP>:8787  (e.g. http://192.168.4.24:8787)
#
# The default points at the DEPLOYED backend, so a fresh clone runs against something
# real without anyone first standing up a server. Override it in .env.local (gitignored)
# when you want to develop against localhost — `npm run dev-client` writes that for you.
#
# Backend secrets (OAuth client ids/secrets, BROWSER_RUNTIME_URL, etc.) belong in the
# repo-root server .env — NOT here.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://homeops-ai.onrender.com/
